~ scene1
[i]He sits at the precipice of the world, as ever. Countless ends it has met, and into countless shapes it has been moulded.[/i]
[i]Death and rebirth. Cycle after cycle. A world unable to breathe.[/i]
[i]Every reality has sprawled out before my eyes.[/i]
[i]It was time. I took it all in. I found comfort in the sight I had etched into my mind.[/i]
[i]That of the tempest. Bolts of lightning shearing down across the horizon. A razorwind cutting across the glade. The brilliance of the flames that spew forth. The capacity for such beauty to raze so wholly. A poignant world.[/i]
